   "subject": "fix: adversarial-review round on the Tier-A batch \u2014 8 findings fixed (Codex gpt-5.6 #1-#5,#7,#8,#10,#12)",
   "body": "The review materially saved two fixes: F6's fingerprint included the\ndaily-retrained blend sha (box-verified: changes every pick day) and would\nhave shipped dead \u2014 now (policy_npz_sha256, feature_env_hash); and F1's\nloop-closure had a terminal escape through present_unverified \u2014 now only an\nexact match is terminal, and a missing slot count is a mismatch regardless\nof crosswalk gaps. Also: multi-horizon churn windows catch slow crash\nloops; new WARN sources wired into always-attention (they were\njournal-only); per-file OSError propagates in lookback scans; cutoff\nboundary excludes first_pitch-5 exactly; churn state hardened; --dry-run no\nlonger mutates live state. Deferred with rationale in the audit doc:\npostponed-game awareness (product call), pre-existing lookback off-by-one,\nDM outbox (YAGNI).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
